From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: orangepi6 kernel-7 port
Subject: [PATCH] hwmon scmi enable sensors by id and keep thermal zones

7.x enables each SCMI temperature sensor with SENSOR_CONFIG_SET before
registering its thermal zone, but passes the position in the temperature
array instead of the sensor id, and skips the thermal zone when the call
fails. The Sky1 firmware rejects it (err=-2 for every sensor), so no SCMI
thermal zones were registered. Use sensor->id, and keep registering the
thermal zone when enabling fails, as 6.18 did.
---
 drivers/hwmon/scmi-hwmon.c | 15 ++++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/hwmon/scmi-hwmon.c b/drivers/hwmon/scmi-hwmon.c
index eec223d17..30bd9ec48 100644
--- a/drivers/hwmon/scmi-hwmon.c
+++ b/drivers/hwmon/scmi-hwmon.c
@@ -341,12 +341,17 @@ static int scmi_hwmon_probe(struct scmi_device *sdev)
 		if (!sensor)
 			continue;
 
-		ret = sensor_ops->config_set(ph, i, sensor_config);
-		if (ret) {
-			dev_err(dev, "Error enabling sensor %s. err=%d\n",
+		/*
+		 * Enable the sensor by its SCMI id, not by its position in
+		 * the temperature array. Firmware that does not support
+		 * SENSOR_CONFIG_SET (or has the sensor always on) answers
+		 * with an error; keep registering the thermal zone then, as
+		 * older kernels did.
+		 */
+		ret = sensor_ops->config_set(ph, sensor->id, sensor_config);
+		if (ret)
+			dev_dbg(dev, "Could not enable sensor %s. err=%d\n",
 				sensor->name, ret);
-			continue;
-		}
 
 		/*
 		 * Warn on any misconfiguration related to thermal zones but
